nt the end of april for the  fellows game the start of march  for the budget it potentially means that  the chancellor can it start to introduce  measures in that march budget  that try to get the economy going again  in time for the photo scheme to come to  an end so people don't start to lay off  their workers uh before uh will they  learn basically what kind of support  there's gonna be whether it's gonna be  tax cuts or spending  increases but i think finally when you  kind of take an overarching sense of  what we're learning about  uh from the treasury it is the sense  that many of these restrictions  that we've been hearing about today are  likely to continue well into the new  year  and as a result of that the government  thinks that more economic support is  going to be necessary not just  for the first few weeks and months of  next year but potentially all the way  into the middle of the spring  towards the end of april underlining  just how concerned they are  that there will continue to be  disruption to the economy as a result  of covert 19. so i think a lot to dig  into it in terms of the subtext  but the substantial news is an extension  of the furlough scheme  and that idea that the 80 was going to  be reduced well that's  off the table for the time being
 

